    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on several high-upside matchups today, led by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 83.29 efficiency score makes him the clear centerpiece of the offense. Facing Rea, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a potent combination of a favorable park and a favorable pitcher matchup, with his dynamic platoon advantage and lead-off spot pushing his floor significantly higher than the field. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.55) are elite starts; both benefit from sub-5.00 xERA opposition and strong lineup positioning, maximizing their potential for both counting stats and stolen base opportunities, which remain our primary priority for the 5x5 format.\n\nWe are forced to navigate a few high-risk profiles, specifically with **Heliot Ramos** (43.98) and **Josh Lowe** (41.90). **Heliot Ramos** faces the formidable Cease and a sub-3.00 xERA, effectively neutralizing his lead-off advantage. Meanwhile, the benching of **Miguel Vargas** remains the most difficult decision of the day. Despite a stellar 53.40 score and an elite 0.406 xwOBA, **Miguel Vargas** just missed the cut because the current starting configuration\u2014particularly with **Jacob Wilson** and **Cole Carrigg**\u2014offered slightly better positional efficiency. We are monitoring the **Josh Lowe** situation closely; while he is currently active, his low score due to the platoon disadvantage against Gore is concerning, and he remains the most likely candidate to be swapped if official lineups shift.",
